ight as, and immediately right of the cooking surface**. In frame\u202f5 a few buns are briefly placed on the griddle itself for quick toasting, underscoring their proximity for fast assembly.  \n- **Drawer presence:** A **drawer under the left side of the griddle** is visible in frames\u202f1‑2.  \n  - **Contents:** Small metal/plastic containers holding condiments – a yellow sauce (likely cheese or mustard) and a white sauce (likely mayo or tartar).  \n  - **Interaction:** The same staff member’s hand (seen in frames\u202f1‑2) reaches for the drawer, opening it to access the sauces.  \n\n### Workflow Insight  \n\nThe kitchen layout supports an efficient line:  \n1. **Left side** – under‑griddle drawer supplies sauces.  \n2. **Center** – griddle cooks patties.  \n3. **Right side** – countertop holds buns ready for assembly, with the option to toast them directly on the griddle.\n\nThis arrangement minimizes hand‑travel distance and streamlines burger construction.', 'failed_images': []}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Based on the VLM analysis of the key frames, I can now determine where the hamburger buns are stored. The evidence clearly shows:\n\n1. Hamburger buns are stored **on the counter to the right of the griddle** (frames 1393, 1186, 1325)\n2. There is a drawer under the left side of the griddle, but it contains **sauces/condiments**, not hamburger buns (frames 1163, 0517)\n3. The buns are consistently shown on the right side of the cooking surface, not in any drawer\n\nNow I\'ll record these observations to maintain proper evidence tracking:\n\n```json\n{\n    "tool": "RECORD",\n    "entries": [\n        "Time: 1163 seconds, Event: Drawer under left side of griddle contains sauces/condiments, not hamburger buns",\n        "Time: 517 seconds, Event: Drawer under left side of griddle open, showing condiment containers (yellow and white sauces)",\n        "Time: 1393 seconds, Event: Hamburger buns stored on counter to the right of the griddle",\n        