g, and moving buns on the griddle (e.g., Frame 4, 5, 6, 18, 19).\n\n✅ **Spatial relationship between buns and iron plate/griddle**  \nThis is the key criterion. The buns being **cooked** are on the griddle itself (left side in Frame 4, center in Frame 5). The **uncooked buns** (which might be considered “stored” for immediate use) are visible in stacks on a tray or shelf **to the right of the griddle** (e.g., Frame 4, 9, 10, 20). However, this is not a “storage location” in the sense of a drawer or container — it’s a prep area.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Evaluation:\n\nThe question asks: **“Where are the hamburger buns stored?”**  \nThe answer “On the right side of the iron plate” implies that the buns are stored in a location to the right of the griddle. While uncooked buns are *located* there, they are not *stored* there — they are staged for immediate cooking. “Stored” suggests a dedicated, organized storage space (like a drawer, bin, or shelf), not a temporary prep area.\n\nMoreover, in Frame 12 and 22, we see a separate, smaller griddle/flat-top to the left of the main griddle — and buns are also toasted there. This further complicates the spatial claim.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion:\n\nThe answer **‘1’ is incorrect** because:\n- The buns are not shown being *stored* — only being *cooked* or *staged*.\n- The location “on the right side of the iron plate” refers to a prep tray, not a storage unit.\n- The term “stored” implies a more permanent or organized containment, which is not visually supported.\n\n✅ **Final Verdict: Answer ‘1’ is NOT correct.**'}], 'formatted_responses': ["\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/O14bbpvy2x0/frames/frame_0512.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/O14bbpvy2x0/frames/frame_0513.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/O14bbpvy2x0/frames/frame_0514.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/O14bbpvy2x0/frames/frame_0515.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/O14bbpvy2x0/frames/fr